  "body": "This PR adds mutations to an image element's `referrerpolicy` attribute to the list of [relevant mutations](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/images.html#relevant-mutations). This should be the only spec work required to close #5244.\n\nWe could also mention the `referrerpolicy` attribute in [this example](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/images.html#updating-the-image-data:attr-img-crossorigin-2) but I don't think it is required, so I'm happy leaving it as-is, since the example text doesn't cover all relevant mutations anyways.\n\n- [x] At least two implementers are interested (and none opposed):\n   * Chrome\n   * Firefox already re-fetches images when `img.referrerPolicy` is changed (but I haven't tested Firefox against my WIP WPTs)\n- [x] [Tests](https://github.com/web-platform-tests/wpt) are written and can be reviewed and commented upon at:\n   * https://github.com/web-platform-tests/wpt/pull/23309 (reviewed at https://crrev.com/c/2171816)\n- [x] [Implementation bugs](https://github.com/whatwg/meta/blob/master/MAINTAINERS.md#handling-pull-requests) are filed:\n   * Chrome: https://bugs.chromium.org/p/chromium/issues/detail?id=1061685\n   * Firefox: https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=1633939\n   * Safari: https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=209970\n\n\n<!--\n    This comment and the below content is programatically generated.\n    You may add a comma-separated list of anchors you'd like a\n    direct link to below (e.g. #idl-serializers, #idl-sequence):\n\n    Don't remove this comment or modify anything below this line.\n    If you don't want a preview generated for this pull request,\n    just replace the whole of this comment's content by \"no preview\"\n    and remove what's below.\n-->\n***\n<a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/5434/images.html\" title=\"Last updated on Apr 28, 2020, 11:49 PM UTC (4fbcd8a)\">/images.html</a>  ( <a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/5434/d160aea...4fbcd8a/images.html\" title=\"Last updated on Apr 28, 2020, 11:49 PM UTC (4fbcd8a)\">diff</a> )",
